From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Chad Cormier Roussel <chadcormierroussel@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 15:28:55 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] IR: a memory load the program doesn't use still faults

LoadMem and LoadMemTSO had no side effects, so the dead-code pass
dropped a load once nothing used its value, and with it the fault an
x86 memory operand raises on an unmapped address. HotSpot's interpreter
null-checks a receiver with `cmp (%reg),%rax` and ignores the flags: the
fault is the check. Under FEX the compare went, a null receiver reached
the method, and its first field load faulted where the JVM expects none
(3DMark's Java backend died in String.trim() after every benchmark).
Both loads are side-effecting now.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
index 8805200..3136fdf 100644
--- a/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
+++ b/FEXCore/Source/Interface/IR/IR.json
@@ -530,7 +530,10 @@
       },
 
       "SSA = LoadMem RegisterClass:$Class, OpSize:#Size, GPR:$Addr, GPR:$Offset, OpSize:$Align, MemOffsetType:$OffsetType, u8:$OffsetScale": {
+        "Desc": ["Loads from memory. Kept when nothing uses the value: an x86 memory operand faults on an unmapped address",
+                 "whatever happens to what it read (HotSpot's null check is a cmp whose flags nothing reads)"],
         "Inline": ["", "Mem"],
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "DestSize": "Size"
       },
 
@@ -575,9 +578,11 @@
       },
 
       "SSA = LoadMemTSO RegisterClass:$Class, OpSize:#Size, GPR:$Addr, GPR:$Offset, OpSize:$Align, MemOffsetType:$OffsetType, u8:$OffsetScale": {
-        "Desc": ["Does a x86 TSO compatible load from memory. Offset must be Invalid()."
+        "Desc": ["Does a x86 TSO compatible load from memory. Offset must be Invalid().",
+                 "Kept when nothing uses the value, as LoadMem is: the fault is the x86 operand's side effect."
                 ],
         "Inline": ["", "Memtso"],
+        "HasSideEffects": true,
         "DestSize": "Size"
       },
 
